Description: fontconfig's bundled config: random_r and GNU strerror_r are glibc's
 Chromium's copy of fontconfig carries one config header for Linux, made
 on glibc, which says the system has random_r and initstate_r and the GNU
 strerror_r (returning a string). musl has neither random_r (fontconfig
 then uses random()) nor the GNU strerror_r (its strerror_r is POSIX's,
 which fontconfig also knows): said only on glibc.
Forwarded: not-needed (Jam OS's; Linux builds use glibc, Alpine the
 system's fontconfig)
---
--- a/third_party/fontconfig/include/meson-config.h
+++ b/third_party/fontconfig/include/meson-config.h
@@ -74,3 +74,5 @@

+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
 #define HAVE_GNU_STRERROR_R 1
+#endif

@@ -98,7 +100,9 @@

 #define HAVE_RANDOM 1

+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
 #define HAVE_RANDOM_R 1
+#endif

 #define HAVE_RAND_R 1

